{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/362621-the-river-of-death-and-other-byways-connection-with-the-shadowlands","id":362621,"title":"The River of Death and other Byways: connection with the Shadowlands","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-07T10:28:14-08:00","id":362621,"title":"The River of Death and other Byways: connection with the Shadowlands","content":"If I got things correctly, the River of Death and other well-kept Byways once led directly to the Shadowlands, but since the 3rd Great Maelstrom they have been disconnected from it.<br /> <br /> But how did they reach the Shadowlands before? There was a time before the Tempest came to be, and it was called the Darkness, when it was simply continuous with the Shadowlands, instead of &quot;under&quot; it? How did you reach the Darkness then, besides using a Nihil? Could you walk to the &quot;end&quot; of the Shadowlands (maybe to a remote area, a cave or the ocean, or a river), and eventually you would be on the River of Death, or some Byway, that then took you further into the Underworld?<br /> <br /> Or I got it wrong and these were never connected to the Shadowlands? Stygia uses Tempest Portals; were these always the standard form of access to the Tempest, especially at a time when Nihils were supposed to be more rare?<br /> <br /> And at the delta of the River of Death lies Stygia, but does it have a source? Does the River of Death &quot;begin&quot; at some point? What would happen if one would travel it upstream?<br /> <br /> I know many of these questions have never been answered in the Books (yet, the Book of Oblivion wil hopefully shed some light on these). But what do you think or have come up with on your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T12:10:55-08:00","id":362773,"title":"","content":"I always imagined them as being colocal with certain known rivers and roads. They look like a landmark you've seen dozens of times before but walk or sail down them just the right way, or get distracted at the wrong time, and you'll be on a path out of the shadowlands and into the deeper underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T06:46:22-08:00","id":363454,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">The following response is \u201cto my understanding:\u201d</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/362621-the-river-of-death-and-other-byways-connection-with-the-shadowlands#post362621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But how did they reach the Shadowlands before? There was a time before the Tempest came to be, and it was called the Darkness, when it was simply continuous with the Shadowlands, instead of &quot;under&quot; it?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Not quite. In this era, the Darkness and the Shadowlands were still separate. In fact, some parts of the Darkness were more distinguishable than they are now. Before the Tempest, the Sea of Shadows (the area around the Labyrinth), the Sunless Sea (between Stygia and the Far Shores), and the Sea of Souls (the area of the Sunless Sea that surrounds Stygia) had more definition between each other. After the Third Great Maelstrom, the \u201cweather\u201d became a permanent and horrible storm; in the modern era, it\u2019s not inaccurate to simply refer to all three areas as \u201cThe Tempest.\u201d </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/362621-the-river-of-death-and-other-byways-connection-with-the-shadowlands#post362621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How did you reach the Darkness then, besides using a Nihil? Could you walk to the &quot;end&quot; of the Shadowlands (maybe to a remote area, a cave or the ocean, or a river), and eventually you would be on the River of Death, or some Byway, that then took you further into the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">You reached the Darkness then the same way you reach the Tempest now: Byways and Channels. Byways/Channels lead through the different levels of the Underworld, including the Shadowlands. The River of Death is the Grand High Poobah of Byways. Where it starts, I have no idea\u2026 </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T09:57:39-08:00","id":363614,"title":"","content":"But if the Darkness and the Shadowlands were places apart, how did Byways connect with it? Assuming one could consider a Byway a place within the Tempest that connected with the Shadowlands. And are they still connected now, after the 3rd Great Maelstrom? Or the separation of Stygia from the Shadowlands means exactly the separation of the Byways from Shadowlands?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/362621-the-river-of-death-and-other-byways-connection-with-the-shadowlands?p=363454#post363454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">You reached the Darkness then the same way you reach the Tempest now: Byways and Channels. </span><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But one does not reach the Tempest through a Byway or Channel, but through a Nihil or a Tempest portal (which seems to be a form of Nihil). Byways and Channels are used to navigate the Tempest, not access it. That was always my understanding.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/362621-the-river-of-death-and-other-byways-connection-with-the-shadowlands?p=363454#post363454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Byways/Channels lead through the different levels of the Underworld, including the Shadowlands. </span><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If Byways/Channels (places which do not exist in the Skinlands) are connected to the Shadowlands, which is a reflection of the living world, then how do these Byways/Channels look like? As Ramnesis suggested, you suddnely are in a place that doesn't connect with another place in the Skinlands anymore, marking the entrance to the Tempest?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T18:07:12-08:00","id":363958,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I was skimming through <i>Sea of Shadows</i> and \u2013Frick!- you\u2019re right; Byways are used to get through the Tempest. The whole \u201cShadowlands Byway\u201d thing, I think, was one of the many House Rules my troupe used. I offer my apologies for not being as helpful as I thought. (It\u2019s been a while \u2013 RAW and HRs kinda blend together in my faulty memory.)<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll dig more through <i>Sea of Shadows</i> and <i>Wraith</i> (first and second) to help give you a more official answer. In the meantime, here\u2019s a brief version of some House fluff about traversing the different tiers of the Underworld. It worked well enough for my troupe, but \u2013 you know \u2013 YMMV. <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Byways that exist in the Shadowlands can take intrepid Wraiths further into the Underworld. Some are marked by Harbingers and others or not. Usually far removed from Necropoli, anyone with some working knowledge of Argos can tell the difference between a Shadowlands road and a Byway proper. Most Harbingers describe the experience as hearing the distant (but audible) sound of the Tempest when on a Shadowlands Byway.</span><br /> <br /> I think we had some crossroads that temporarily became Byways at midnight. I remember the idea being really cool, but I can\u2019t find anything in RAW to substantiate it, so I\u2019m assuming that was another wonky house rule. <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I\u2019ll repost (hopefully) soon after I finish digging. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T09:03:03-08:00","id":364455,"title":"","content":"Hi guys. Sorry in advance for my level of English, but I couldn't resist to join the conversation and give you my two oboli.<br /> Everything stated below is just my personal interpretation. But before I start, note that like everybody else I'm talking to my understanding, which is in my opinion already an answer to your question: there may be NO definite answer...<br /> <br /> Your question leads somehow to the geography of the underworld, where does the Tempest starts, how do the Byways/Channels appear when they reach the Shadowlands, etc.<br /> In the universe of WtO, like in other universes set in the 'world of the deads', the geopgraphy is volontarily 'not understandable' from human standards. A line I found in the WtO novel 'Caravan of Shadows' (page 209) sum it up quite well in my opinion (quote from a specter): '<i>You musn't think of the Tempest as some boring piece of solid, three-dimensional earthly real estate. It's more like a four- or five-dimensional cloud in a constant state of flux, and at any given moment, I know all the shortcuts</i> (...)'.<br /> <br /> So to answer the question 'How do the Byways/Channels connect to the Shadowlands?': it can obviously be through Nihils. These can only open sometimes under certain conditions, or always be opened, but basically it is a 'regular' Nihil connected to the Tempest but with a cobbled way going through it and that was once built by the Hierarchy until Stygia, or a Nihil that for instance leads you directly into one of the many rivers of death. Byways are made out of souls, out of memories that can resist to the evermoving Tempest. They are for the huge majority of them cobbled ways and they start directly inside the different Necropoli. I see them starting from the gates of the historical core of Quick cities. But where do they lead exactly? Most of them through Nihils actually, see why below.<br /> <br /> Before getting further, I think it's important to mention the 'bondaries' between the Shadowlands and the Tempest. Knowing the Shadowlands are, like Stygia, like the Far Shores, floatting inside/on it. So where do the winds of maelstroms that smashe Necropoli come from? In other words... where does exactly the Tempest start from the Shadowlands point of view? My answer to this question is (on top of Nihils): everywhere no human beings ever lived, ever once formed memories out of the place. Or really long time ago, the memories being now lost in the Tempest. Typically all the oceans, but also all the places really remote from civilisation, like the 'middles' of deserts or big forests. Of course, the sky above the Shadowlands as I picture it is also one of these bondaries.<br /> <br /> So if you follow a Byway and if it doesn't go through a Nihil at some point*, it can be really really long to follow. And if it doesn't lead you through an ocean at some point, then the more you leave 'civilisation' i.e. places of the Shadowlands not inhabited by a lot of Quicks, far from Necropoli, the more the Shadowlands are decayed and covered with the mist that was there everywhere before the third great maelstrom. Like an 'external' layer of the Tempest, this mist becomes more and more windy as you keep going through places less and less remembered, more and more prey to Oblivion. These remote and misty areas are also where you can find the 'source', the beginning of Channels that will lead you throught the Tempest. Note that you can find such misty areas between two inhabited places but without any link to the Tempest.<br /> <br /> *Because Byways have been mostly built at a period of time prior to mankind expansion on earth, it's more than likely than what was then a 'bondary' with the mist/Tempest is now an inhabited place, resulting in a byway going through a Nihil.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4701-dam","name":"Dam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T10:55:41-08:00","id":365534,"title":"","content":"Thank you Dam, for sharing these ideas. It is quite simple and elegant actually to picture Byways reaching the Shadowlands through Nihils that may be open only in certain circumstances (like in a crossroad at midnight, as suggested by Nazfool). I think you got it right here, even if it is not something in the books. Also, I like what you wrote about the relationship remote areas of the Shadowlands might have with the Tempest, as I was also imagining something similar.<br /> <br /> Where did you get the &quot;mist&quot; part as a feature of the remote areas of the Tempest? I realized I also picture these mists, but cannot recall where I read about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T05:17:17-08:00","id":366202,"title":"","content":"I tried to find a quote in one of the books about the third great maelstrom transforming the 'mist' that incarnated the Darkness into the Tempest as Wraiths know it nowadays.<br /> Well, I failed. But I wouldn't have come with this idea from nowhere, maybe in one of the European add-ons such as 'World of Darkness: France'...<br /> <br /> Anyway, everyone would agree that the third maelstrom made the Tempest stormy, turbulent, therefore that it wasn't the case before, and the separation of Stygia from the Shadowlands must also be understood in terms of difficulty/impossibility to walk the Byways because of that. Of course the clouds of the Tempest are not made of condensed watter like regular clouds, but the physical fog and the mist are nothing else than a 'very low altittude cloud', and a lot of stories, movies and even video games present the underworld, the limbo as covered by fog. It's a popular imagery.<br /> <br /> Last but not the least, if the clouds of the Tempest were once closer to a mist, than for me it makes sense than the surroundings of the Tempest still present this form, the strengh of Oblivion being there weakened/calmed by the close 'life': the start of the Shadowlands or of any far shores.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4701-dam","name":"Dam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T20:08:12-07:00","id":527263,"title":"","content":"My belief was the Darkness lay under the Shadowlands and the main Byway of the River of Death came from the Skinlands, leading through the Shadowlands to go down into the Darkness until it spread out to Stygia and the Far Shores.<br /> Before the 4th Maelstrom struck, railroads and new roads were being constructed, the Grim and Skeletal Legions were spreading Heirarchy Citadels amongst the Necropoli that had sprung up in the American frontier days. This was from the 1890s to the 4th Maelstrom and was the days when the Midnight Express came to be. Although these roads and railways are newer and constructed, they're still classed as Byways as they do the same job as them. As the Legionnaires had to move with the Skinland people they were assigned to, it's no reason to doubt that the roads and railways constructed through the Shadowlands by them look too different from the Skinlands equivalents, though likely they are made from Stygian and Soulsteel as Thralls were forced into extensive mining back in those days and when burnt out from it and fatigued, <i>they</i> got thrown into the furnaces and smelted down too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T16:33:02-07:00","id":538909,"title":"","content":"It's not canon, but real world mythology linked certain places as <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gates_of_hell\" target=\"_blank\">entrances of the underworld</a>. Usually they were caves of some kind - sometimes volcanic, sometimes with underground springs - that just lead deeper and deeper into the Earth. I'd use such places as &quot;natural&quot; entrances to the River of Death and other Byways. Besides the ones famous for it, I'm sure the ST can develop whatever he needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}